{"path":"io/iostream_category","title":"std::iostream_category","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>iostream_category","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/iostream_category","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"Obtains a reference to the static error category object for iostream errors. The object is required to override the virtual function error_category::name() to return a pointer to the string \"iostream\".","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/ios\">&lt;ios&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_category\"><span class=\"kw875\">std::<span class=\"me2\">error_category</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> iostream_category<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Obtains a reference to the static error category object for iostream errors. The object is required to override the virtual function <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">error_category<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">name</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> to return a pointer to the string <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"st0\">\"iostream\"</span></span></code>. It is used to identify error codes provided in the exceptions of type <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/failure\">std::ios_base::failure</a></span>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>A reference to the static object of unspecified runtime type, derived from <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/error_category\">std::error_category</a></span>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;fstream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ifstream\"><span class=\"kw1749\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ifstream</span></span></a> f<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"doesn't exist\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">try</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        f.<span class=\"me1\">exceptions</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>f.<span class=\"me1\">failbit</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">catch</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/failure\"><span class=\"kw1687\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ios_base</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">failure</span></span></a><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> e<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Caught an ios_base::failure.<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>\n                  <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Error code: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> e.<span class=\"me1\">code</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">value</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> \n                  <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" (\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> e.<span class=\"me1\">code</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">message</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\")<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>\n                  <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Error category: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> e.<span class=\"me1\">code</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">category</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">name</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Caught an ios_base::failure.\nError code: 1 (unspecified iostream_category error)\nError category: iostream</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue2087\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 2087</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++11\n</td>\n<td><code>iostream_category</code> was not declared <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>declared <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span></span>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/failure\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>failure</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  stream exception <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member class of <code>std::ios_base</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/io_errc\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>io_errc</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  the IO stream error codes <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(enum)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::iostream_category","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++11. Obtains a reference to the static error category object for iostream errors."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"A reference to the static object of unspecified runtime type, derived from std::error_category."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"failure","note":"stream exception"},{"label":"io_errc","note":"the IO stream error codes"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":183,"codeBlockCount":2}
